{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1110","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1110","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1110\",\"parent_revision\":\"0b9f24c3633e2b98aef7edc0c83579e281858b0b\",\"root_revision\":\"6a4bfb3bcec8ede52b795c7f95bd5a16b5508fe7675f736ebeb2c8d7e067e18f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAPPROVED-WITH-GAPS (2026-04-15)\\\\n\\\\nFunctional intent and target behavior are clearly stated. Primary dependency is #1109 (known backlog item, not unknown gap).\\\\n\\\\nConditions:\\\\n1. HookProfile.STRICT exists in codebase | AVAILABLE | task_status_hook.py lines 90-99 \u2014 defined; resolved in main(); no strict PostToolUse branch yet\\\\n2. JSONL telemetry file schema (behavioral-{session_id}.jsonl) | AVAILABLE (dependent) | #1109 groomed content defines schema \u2014 available once #1109 ships\\\\n3. behavioral_summary.py shift score computation | AVAILABLE (dependent) | #1109 creates the script \u2014 available once #1109 ships\\\\n4. CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD env var | MISSING | grep across full codebase: zero matches for this variable; stated in item description only\\\\n5. Hook timeout budget for JSONL read + score computation | DERIVABLE | hooks.json PostToolUse timeout 10s; JSONL read + shift score expected < 50ms\\\\n6. stderr output format for drift warning | AVAILABLE | item description states exact format matching existing hook stderr convention\\\\n\\\\nMISSING count: 1 (CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD env var \u2014 definition, default, and parsing location unspecified)\\\\nDERIVABLE count: 1 (timeout budget)\\\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\\\n\\\\nRequired unblock actions:\\\\n- Confirm whether behavioral_summary.py (from #1109) will expose a callable Python function (not CLI-only)\\\\n- Human confirmation on default threshold value (see Questions for Human)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 HookProfile.STRICT exists and SubagentStop uses it, but PostToolUse has no strict-mode behavior. Activating strict mode changes SubagentStop but has no observable effect on PostToolUse. Gap is real but lower urgency than #1109, which provides the telemetry infrastructure and must ship first.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Developers running strict-mode sessions cannot detect in-session behavioral drift from PostToolUse events. The JSONL telemetry will exist (after #1109) but the shift detection and warning path will not fire.\\\\n- Bottleneck: `HookProfile.STRICT` is named and partially implemented \u2014 SubagentStop has a strict handler but PostToolUse does not. Strict mode is asymmetric until this item ships.\\\\n- Affects: All developers using `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict` who expect real-time drift detection during sessions.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Closes the strict-mode PostToolUse gap: after #1109, the only missing strict-mode behavior is the in-session drift warning.\\\\n- Real-time signal: unlike behavioral_summary.py (post-session analysis), this provides an in-session warning the orchestrator can act on immediately.\\\\n- Configurable threshold: CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD allows operators to tune sensitivity without code changes.\\\\n- Closes the compression-monitor integration described in research/ai-observability/compression-monitor.md.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict and a PostToolUse (Write|Edit|Bash) event fires:\\\\n\\\\n1. The hook reads the last N records from ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/telemetry/behavioral-{session_id}.jsonl (created by #1109).\\\\n2. A behavioral shift score is computed from those records using the same windowing logic as behavioral_summary.py.\\\\n3. If the shift score exceeds CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD (default: 0.3), the hook writes to stderr: [hook] behavioral drift detected: shift_score={score:.3f} (threshold={threshold})\\\\n4. If the shift score is at or below the threshold, no output is emitted.\\\\n5. The existing LastActivity timestamp update still executes regardless of profile.\\\\n6. A drift warning in stderr does not cause the hook to exit non-zero \u2014 it is observational, not a block.\\\\n7. When fewer records exist than the minimum window size (N/2), the hook skips computation and emits no warning (insufficient data).\\\\n\\\\nWhen CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE is standard or unset: the drift-score computation is not performed; PostToolUse behavior is identical to before this item.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nWhen done, the following is observable:\\\\n\\\\n- task_status_hook.py PostToolUse handler has a branch: when profile is STRICT, it reads the behavioral JSONL file and computes a shift score.\\\\n- CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD env var is recognized by the hook: os.environ.get('CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD', '0.3') or equivalent is present.\\\\n- Running a session with CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD=0.01 and triggering Write calls with varied response lengths produces [hook] behavioral drift detected messages on stderr.\\\\n- Running the same session under CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=standard produces no drift messages.\\\\n- Unit tests exist that feed a synthetic JSONL file to the strict PostToolUse handler and verify: (a) warning emitted when shift score exceeds threshold, (b) no warning when below threshold, (c) no warning when insufficient records.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. With HOOK_PROFILE=strict and JSONL shift score > 0.3: stderr contains [hook] behavioral drift detected: shift_score=... (threshold=0.3)\\\\n2. With HOOK_PROFILE=strict and JSONL shift score <= 0.3: no drift warning on stderr\\\\n3. With HOOK_PROFILE=standard or unset: drift-score computation is not performed\\\\n4. With HOOK_PROFILE=strict and fewer records than minimum window size: no warning, hook exits 0\\\\n5. With CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD=0.5: threshold used is 0.5, not 0.3\\\\n6. Exception inside drift scoring path (JSONL missing, malformed line): hook does not exit non-zero\\\\n7. LastActivity timestamp update completes even when drift warning is emitted\\\\n8. Unit tests cover all four cases: above-threshold, below-threshold, insufficient-records, JSONL-missing\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Hook impl | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py |\\\\n| Hook config | plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json |\\\\n| Path utils | plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py |\\\\n| Upstream #1109 | Behavioral fingerprint tracking in PostToolUse hook |\\\\n| Related #1111 | Vocabulary canary list for constraint persistence after compression |\\\\n| Research | research/ai-observability/compression-monitor.md |\\\\n| Test | tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #1109 \\\"Behavioral fingerprint tracking in PostToolUse hook\\\" must ship first. Creates the JSONL telemetry file, behavioral_summary.py, and dh_paths.telemetry_dir(). Without these, this item has no data to score.\\\\n- Blocks: Any mid-session alerting or session-checkpoint tooling that reacts to the [hook] behavioral drift detected stderr signal.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall (0.5-1 day) \u2014 the hook plumbing already exists. HookProfile.STRICT branch pattern is established by run_strict_pre_completion_checks in the same file. This item adds: JSONL read + windowed shift score computation + threshold comparison + conditional stderr write inside the PostToolUse strict branch. CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD env var parsing is a 1-liner.\\\\n\\\\nEffort depends on whether the shift score logic is imported from behavioral_summary.py (smaller \u2014 reuse) or replicated inline (slightly larger). Test coverage for the new branch is straightforward given existing test patterns in tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py.\\\\n\\\\nGated: this item cannot start until #1109 is complete.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- #1109 not yet shipped: the JSONL telemetry infrastructure does not exist. This item cannot be implemented until #1109 is complete.\\\\n- Shift score API undefined: not yet decided whether the strict PostToolUse handler will import behavioral_summary.py as a Python module, replicate the windowing logic inline, or call it as a subprocess. This design choice affects test strategy and coupling between items.\\\\n- CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD: env var name confirmed in item description, but the parsing location and type conversion (float) are not yet established in any code path.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail\\\\nRationale: HookProfile.STRICT exists and SubagentStop has a strict handler (run_strict_pre_completion_checks), but the PostToolUse handler has no strict-mode code path. The infrastructure is in place (HookProfile enum, profile resolution, hook wiring) but the behavioral signal that would surface compression-induced drift is never computed in the PostToolUse path under any profile. This is a structural gap in the strict profile, not a logic error in existing code.\\\\nScenario Target: Long-running session with context compression event, CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict set, behavioral drift occurring after compression boundary \u2014 drift goes undetected because the strict PostToolUse branch does not exist.\\\\nAnalysis Method: Structural gap analysis \u2014 codebase confirms HookProfile.STRICT defined, SubagentStop branch exists, PostToolUse strict branch does not exist.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the strict PostToolUse drift check import behavioral_summary.py as a Python module (coupling the two scripts), or replicate the last-N-window shift score logic inline (keeping the hook self-contained)?\\\\n- Is the default threshold of 0.3 correct for PostToolUse strict mode, or should it differ from the compression-monitor Behavioral Footprint HIGH threshold?\\\\n- Should drift warnings on stderr be sufficient, or should the hook also append a structured {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"drift_warning\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"shift_score\\\\\\\": ...} record to the telemetry JSONL for post-session analysis?\\\\n- How many records (N) should constitute the minimum window before the hook is confident enough to compute a score? The item description does not specify N.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a new additive feature, not a defect. No failure condition to reproduce prior to implementation.\\\\n\\\\nMeasurable signal: with `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict` set and #1109 shipped, after a session where the shift score in the JSONL telemetry file exceeds `CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD`, stderr from the PostToolUse hook contains `behavioral drift detected`.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWith `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict` and `CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD=0.3`, after a context compression event, the PostToolUse hook stderr includes `behavioral drift detected` when the shift score exceeds 0.3. Without compression, the message does not appear during normal operation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **real-time behavioral drift scoring in posttooluse strict mode** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/ai-observability/compression-monitor.md -- pattern: PostToolUse real-time drift alerts and behavioral shift scoring\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe PostToolUse hook fires on every Write, Edit, and Bash tool call but only updates a timestamp. No computation is performed on behavioral data. When context compression occurs mid-session, the orchestrator continues with no signal that operational patterns have changed. The hook infrastructure supports the `strict` profile (HookProfile enum with MINIMAL, STANDARD, STRICT) but no strict-mode behavioral check exists for PostToolUse.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict`, the PostToolUse handler computes a rolling behavioral shift score from the last N tool calls (stored in the telemetry JSONL). If the shift score exceeds a configurable threshold, the hook emits a warning via stderr: `[hook] behavioral drift detected: shift_score={score:.3f} (threshold={threshold})`. This warning is visible to the orchestrator and can trigger investigation or session checkpoint behavior. The threshold is configurable via `CLAUDE_SKILLS_DRIFT_THRESHOLD` environment variable (default: 0.3, matching compression-monitor's HIGH threshold).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"61f4bfe9fbca43397591f77a1b3fd4cb17da3b39f13ee0479f480d2f63a5afec\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTcFBQ\"}"}